# JR Anchored — release signing key (SSH allowed-signers format)
#
# This file pins the public key used to sign JR Anchored release tags.
# Format (one signer per line):
#   <principal> <key-type> <public-key>
# e.g.
#   releases@dwylup.com ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAA...
#
# Until a real key is added below, release verification runs in ADVISORY mode:
# admin_update / admin_setup and the GUI will note that signing is not yet
# configured, but will not block. Replace the PLACEHOLDER line with the real
# public key (and publish its fingerprint on www.dwylup.com) to enable
# fail-closed verification.
#
# PLACEHOLDER — release signing key not yet configured
